WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.976
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:16.246 --> 00:17.247
What's going on?

3
00:19.374 --> 00:21.334
The situation's gotten worse.

4
01:22.187 --> 01:23.354
Who are you?

5
01:25.648 --> 01:26.816
I am

6
01:27.525 --> 01:31.154
a senior investigator from the Japan Public Security Intelligence Agency.

7
01:31.237 --> 01:32.947
Kasahara Reina.

8
01:34.824 --> 01:35.992
Since when?

9
01:38.119 --> 01:39.287
From the beginning?

10
01:42.373 --> 01:43.875
As fellow compatriots…

11
01:46.461 --> 01:48.671
I considered you family all these years.

12
01:49.297 --> 01:50.131
You…

13
01:52.217 --> 01:54.844
betrayed our compatriots.

14
01:56.554 --> 01:58.264
Turned them into criminals.

15
02:00.433 --> 02:02.435
People who had nowhere to turn…

16
02:10.526 --> 02:11.611
Kill me.

17
02:17.325 --> 02:18.159
Seo Hyun-tae!

18
02:20.787 --> 02:21.704
Let her go.

19
02:24.123 --> 02:25.375
I said let her go.

20
02:29.254 --> 02:30.421
Ms. Yoon Soo-kyung.

21
02:32.340 --> 02:33.716
I'll leave the rest to you.

22
02:43.351 --> 02:44.435
Stop!

23
02:46.604 --> 02:51.150
Ms. Kasahara, wake up.

24
02:51.234 --> 02:52.068
Hey.

25
02:52.944 --> 02:53.903
Call an ambulance.

26
03:47.999 --> 03:49.834
Hey, Ito!

27
03:50.960 --> 03:52.670
I know you can hear me!

28
04:44.430 --> 04:45.723
Hey, Ito!

29
04:50.645 --> 04:52.980
Hey!

30
04:53.815 --> 04:54.982
Ito!

31
04:58.528 --> 05:00.405
Why won't this thing budge?

32
05:14.085 --> 05:15.420
What the hell is that?

33
05:26.139 --> 05:28.975
Hey, mister! Are you drunk?

34
06:12.560 --> 06:13.561
Good to see you.

35
06:14.729 --> 06:15.897
How…

36
06:24.947 --> 06:26.073
Yoon-ok…

37
06:28.951 --> 06:30.953
sure is a smart one, isn't she?

38
07:25.174 --> 07:26.968
THE BLUE ROAD

39
08:02.169 --> 08:06.090
"One fear breeds infinite fear,

40
08:07.300 --> 08:09.844
and all methods shall be concealed."

41
08:17.018 --> 08:19.020
EMIRI'S BOOK OF MILITARY STRATEGY

42
08:23.274 --> 08:25.067
You're him, right?

43
08:26.402 --> 08:30.364
The man who served my father, now looking after our family's affairs.

44
08:33.826 --> 08:34.827
So it's you.

45
08:35.995 --> 08:38.164
Director Minamoto's boy.

46
08:41.083 --> 08:43.919
Hello, I'm Emi Shunsuke.

47
08:46.380 --> 08:47.298
You're Korean?

48
08:48.758 --> 08:49.884
Or Japanese?

49
08:56.641 --> 08:57.725
Who knows.

50
08:58.643 --> 09:00.478
I'm not really sure myself

51
09:01.312 --> 09:02.688
where I'm from.

52
09:07.860 --> 09:09.278
Ito Makoto.

53
09:20.915 --> 09:23.167
Mr. Seo Hyun-tae of the ANSP Print Shop.

54
09:35.096 --> 09:37.640
There's something you must know going forward.

55
09:44.689 --> 09:46.649
Thanks to you, I'm no longer a cop.

56
09:48.734 --> 09:51.070
So don't be a smartass and give me straight answers.

57
09:52.780 --> 09:55.574
How do you know Hong Du-yeong? Answer me.

58
09:57.201 --> 09:58.035
Well?

59
09:59.704 --> 10:02.748
Did the ANSP kill him and dump his body?

60
10:03.541 --> 10:05.042
I want to hear you say it.

61
10:11.257 --> 10:12.675
Let's see how long you last.

62
10:39.326 --> 10:40.411
How's your partner?

63
10:44.415 --> 10:46.959
She's unconscious, but alive, thankfully.

64
10:48.002 --> 10:49.420
I'm glad she's okay.

65
10:52.798 --> 10:53.841
Here.

66
10:54.717 --> 10:56.594
I found it on Ito's car after he got away.

67
10:56.677 --> 10:57.553
Right.

68
10:59.096 --> 11:01.557
You guys planted this GPS tracker, right?

69
11:04.727 --> 11:07.855
Kim Seok has kidnapped Seo Hyun-tae.

70
11:08.731 --> 11:09.565
What?

71
11:10.065 --> 11:11.525
The truth is,

72
11:11.609 --> 11:15.863
if we failed to arrest him, we were going to use Kim Seok.

73
11:18.574 --> 11:19.950
You're kidding me.

74
11:22.203 --> 11:23.788
Because of you, security service,

75
11:24.455 --> 11:26.582
Detective Kim might end up killing Seo Hyun-tae.

76
11:26.665 --> 11:27.666
First…

77
11:27.750 --> 11:29.126
No, forget it.

78
11:29.210 --> 11:32.004
Where is he now? Surely, you must know.

79
11:34.131 --> 11:34.965
Hey.

80
11:38.135 --> 11:39.428
Answer me.

81
11:40.930 --> 11:42.139
Kowloon Mansions.

82
11:42.223 --> 11:44.475
The two were seen on CCTV,

83
11:44.558 --> 11:47.728
heading to an apartment building where undocumented immigrants live.

84
11:48.395 --> 11:50.189
But please don't worry.

85
11:50.689 --> 11:53.025
Once the local Hong Kong police arrive…

86
11:53.108 --> 11:55.569
It's dangerous, so we have to move together!

87
11:59.740 --> 12:01.158
Detective Kim and I…

88
12:02.117 --> 12:04.078
We may not have worked together for long,

89
12:04.578 --> 12:06.831
but we've been through all sorts in that time.

90
12:09.083 --> 12:10.501
Do you understand what I mean?

91
12:12.962 --> 12:13.879
But…

92
12:24.849 --> 12:26.016
One by one.

93
12:27.268 --> 12:29.186
Let's work through this, step by step.

94
12:30.646 --> 12:32.398
The Print Shop where I was held.

95
12:36.110 --> 12:38.863
It was one of the ANSP's Anti-Communist Investigation Offices

96
12:38.946 --> 12:40.656
used for interrogation and torture.

97
12:41.532 --> 12:42.741
Is that right?

98
13:01.302 --> 13:02.511
I asked if that's right.

99
13:05.306 --> 13:06.307
Yes.

100
13:07.683 --> 13:08.517
Yes, that's right.

101
13:09.560 --> 13:10.519
Next.

102
13:11.312 --> 13:12.563
The original.

103
13:13.689 --> 13:14.899
Twisting…

104
13:16.609 --> 13:19.695
the limbs of corpses was a method devised by the ANSP.

105
13:19.778 --> 13:21.572
And you were a member of the ANSP.

106
13:22.072 --> 13:24.158
What's your connection to the Minamoto family?

107
13:47.431 --> 13:49.433
No one…

108
13:51.477 --> 13:53.145
No one devised it.

109
13:54.939 --> 13:56.315
We never devised it.

110
14:05.491 --> 14:06.784
What do you mean?

111
14:07.826 --> 14:09.203
It just came about.

112
14:12.957 --> 14:13.958
By accident.

113
14:16.669 --> 14:19.213
PRINT SHOP

114
14:19.296 --> 14:20.547
The Print Shop.

115
14:23.092 --> 14:24.718
An organization within the ANSP,

116
14:25.302 --> 14:29.723
made up of hidden North Korean defectors, Korean Chinese, Koryo-saram…

117
14:29.807 --> 14:32.309
People without legal status.

118
14:35.270 --> 14:38.273
REPORT SPIES

119
14:57.501 --> 14:58.836
Our primary duty

120
14:59.920 --> 15:02.047
was to conduct illegal torture.

121
15:04.508 --> 15:06.802
Our director, who trained us in torture,

122
15:08.012 --> 15:10.472
was especially fixated on the anti-Japanese movement.

123
15:13.517 --> 15:16.812
He came from a Japanese family that had remained in Korea

124
15:16.895 --> 15:18.939
after its liberation.

125
15:20.524 --> 15:22.401
His Korean name, Won Seung-il.

126
15:24.445 --> 15:27.156
His Japanese name, Minamoto Shoichi.

127
15:30.325 --> 15:31.618
Later, he went on

128
15:32.411 --> 15:34.371
to build Minamoto Pharmaceuticals.

129
15:37.207 --> 15:38.917
Anyway, that method…

130
15:42.087 --> 15:43.922
Let's stop this here, okay?

131
15:45.674 --> 15:46.967
This is hard on you,

132
15:48.260 --> 15:49.636
and I feel bad too.

133
15:51.472 --> 15:52.890
What are we even doing here?

134
15:53.724 --> 15:57.311
I'm telling you, I really don't know.

135
16:01.231 --> 16:04.109
If you don't know, then what's this?

136
16:05.527 --> 16:07.988
"Japan severed the spirit of the Korean Peninsula,

137
16:08.072 --> 16:10.741
while pro-Japanese collaborators remain in power,

138
16:10.824 --> 16:12.201
mocking our poor citizens."

139
16:16.371 --> 16:18.415
Don't you know our president's policy?

140
16:20.834 --> 16:22.002
Sir.

141
16:22.503 --> 16:23.337
I…

142
16:24.129 --> 16:26.173
I need to go home.

143
16:26.757 --> 16:29.009
I have a wife who's waiting for me

144
16:30.052 --> 16:33.680
and a child who can't do anything without me.

145
16:34.848 --> 16:38.352
Please, I'm begging you.

146
16:39.937 --> 16:41.188
Please.

147
16:55.285 --> 16:56.370
All right.

148
16:58.080 --> 16:59.331
I get it. Now get up.

149
17:08.507 --> 17:09.383
Hey.

150
17:10.300 --> 17:11.343
You bastard!

151
17:14.346 --> 17:15.180
Hey, wait!

152
17:15.264 --> 17:18.183
That's a dead end, you punk!

153
17:20.394 --> 17:21.812
-Hey! -Don't come any closer!

154
17:21.895 --> 17:24.523
I told you, that's a dead end!

155
17:24.606 --> 17:25.649
Hey!

156
17:26.150 --> 17:27.276
Look. I get it.

157
17:27.359 --> 17:28.318
Hey!

158
17:43.750 --> 17:45.460
That was the first time.

159
17:46.378 --> 17:47.629
We

160
17:48.380 --> 17:50.299
had to get rid of the body.

161
17:50.799 --> 17:51.842
So

162
17:52.551 --> 17:54.136
we obliterated the fingerprints

163
17:54.803 --> 17:56.930
and twisted his limbs.

164
17:59.057 --> 18:00.392
We twisted them even more…

165
18:02.603 --> 18:04.313
folded the body up,

166
18:05.981 --> 18:07.858
and dumped it in the sewer.

167
18:20.245 --> 18:21.705
Then, through newspapers and TV,

168
18:23.332 --> 18:26.001
we spread the word that it wasn't our doing…

169
18:28.545 --> 18:30.839
but the work of some civilian murderer.

170
18:33.258 --> 18:34.301
So your director…

171
18:36.303 --> 18:38.513
Minamoto taught you that method?

172
18:40.098 --> 18:41.058
That's right.

173
18:43.435 --> 18:44.645
And we

174
18:45.812 --> 18:47.606
used that method repeatedly.

175
18:49.900 --> 18:52.069
It proved far more useful than we expected.

176
18:54.279 --> 18:56.448
Whenever someone died during a protest…

177
18:58.492 --> 18:59.785
we'd use the same method.

178
19:01.620 --> 19:03.413
We'd dispose of the body the same way.

179
19:08.043 --> 19:10.462
And the ANSP continued to manipulate public opinion.

180
19:12.381 --> 19:14.925
And the papers reporting that they were serial murders

181
19:15.008 --> 19:16.760
would have fueled public fear.

182
19:17.261 --> 19:18.262
That's right.

183
19:19.721 --> 19:21.598
And so, several more died…

184
19:24.393 --> 19:25.936
and several more were dumped.

185
19:28.814 --> 19:30.691
I don't remember all of them…

186
19:33.694 --> 19:36.029
but some of them were just left to rot.

187
19:37.114 --> 19:39.199
And Hong Du-yeong was one of them?

188
19:44.997 --> 19:46.248
Hey, Kim.

189
19:53.338 --> 19:55.299
Hong Du-yeong was my colleague.

190
19:57.509 --> 19:58.552
Your colleague?

191
20:05.976 --> 20:07.769
He was one of us.

192
20:18.613 --> 20:20.949
Hong Du-yeong, the torture specialist.

193
20:36.089 --> 20:37.758
He was one of us.

194
20:43.680 --> 20:46.558
I'm telling you, he was one of us!

195
20:59.404 --> 21:00.489
Bullshit.

196
21:01.198 --> 21:02.783
He was my senior and far…

197
21:04.743 --> 21:07.412
far better at the job than I was.

198
21:08.622 --> 21:10.749
The one I wanted most to be like.

199
21:13.085 --> 21:15.212
The one who taught me everything.

200
21:15.712 --> 21:17.672
The most capable of us.

201
21:18.173 --> 21:19.049
The one I--

202
21:27.682 --> 21:29.476
You expect me to believe that bullshit?

203
21:31.686 --> 21:33.397
Human joints

204
21:34.940 --> 21:36.942
are just like ox sinew.

205
21:38.402 --> 21:40.654
Twist them all you like, but they won't snap.

206
21:40.737 --> 21:42.406
You can stop talking now.

207
21:42.489 --> 21:46.952
That's why you have to wrench them with the intent to tear them apart

208
21:48.245 --> 21:49.996
for them to twist properly.

209
21:52.999 --> 21:55.085
Hong Du-yeong taught me that too.

210
21:59.464 --> 22:01.550
We disposed of so many bodies.

211
22:02.050 --> 22:06.221
How many do you think were never found? Only four are known about, right?

212
22:12.936 --> 22:17.732
Is it now time for me to tell you all about it in detail?

213
22:27.951 --> 22:29.619
I told you to stop.

214
22:31.830 --> 22:33.206
Why? Don't want to hear it?

215
22:34.374 --> 22:35.333
Stop it.

216
22:36.251 --> 22:37.335
Detective Kim!

217
22:44.009 --> 22:45.051
Detective Kim!

218
22:52.809 --> 22:53.935
Kim Seok!

219
22:55.395 --> 22:56.730
If you're going to kill me,

220
22:57.772 --> 22:59.274
I think you'd better do it now.

221
23:02.694 --> 23:03.945
You think I can't kill you?

222
23:05.572 --> 23:06.406
No.

223
23:07.407 --> 23:08.617
Go ahead, then.

224
23:13.622 --> 23:14.789
Come on, do it.

225
23:16.583 --> 23:20.420
Hey, Kim Seok! Detective Kim!

226
23:20.921 --> 23:22.339
You're a cop!

227
23:23.715 --> 23:25.217
You're a cop!

228
23:30.096 --> 23:31.556
We're changing locations first.

229
23:53.578 --> 23:54.454
Why?

230
23:55.622 --> 23:57.123
You don't want to believe it?

231
24:00.085 --> 24:01.753
Is it hard to believe?

232
24:08.343 --> 24:09.719
How about this, then?

233
24:13.723 --> 24:15.141
At the gukbap place.

234
24:24.818 --> 24:26.194
You saw me.

235
24:32.409 --> 24:33.577
Hold on.

236
24:35.787 --> 24:37.038
Who is it?

237
24:37.664 --> 24:39.624
Don't worry. He's a friend of mine.

238
24:40.333 --> 24:41.751
A friend from the Blue Road.

239
24:43.628 --> 24:44.754
Who could he be?

240
24:48.758 --> 24:52.345
Hey, Hyun-tae. It's been a while.

241
24:53.138 --> 24:54.306
You've been well, right?

242
25:05.108 --> 25:06.901
That was the day Uncle Du-yeong died.

243
25:12.449 --> 25:13.783
So you remember.

244
25:41.186 --> 25:42.062
Detective Kim!

245
25:42.937 --> 25:44.022
Are you okay?

246
25:44.981 --> 25:46.441
Answer me!

247
25:46.524 --> 25:47.567
Inose, run away.

248
25:47.651 --> 25:48.610
Get out of here!

249
25:48.693 --> 25:49.903
Detective Kim!

250
26:25.146 --> 26:26.398
Are you sure…

251
26:28.692 --> 26:30.735
you even want to catch me?

252
26:33.488 --> 26:35.407
Is that all you've got?

253
27:28.376 --> 27:30.628
Detective Kim…

254
27:46.478 --> 27:47.896
Where is it?

255
27:47.979 --> 27:48.813
Inose.

256
27:50.565 --> 27:53.234
It's okay, Inose. You're okay.

257
27:53.318 --> 27:55.153
It's okay. It's just a scratch.

258
27:56.946 --> 27:59.115
Inose, answer me.

259
28:13.755 --> 28:14.881
Inose.

260
28:17.509 --> 28:18.676
Say something.

261
28:38.863 --> 28:40.031
Please call an ambulance.

262
28:41.741 --> 28:43.326
We need an ambulance, now.

263
28:50.667 --> 28:53.920
Call an ambulance, quick!

264
28:54.504 --> 28:55.380
An ambulance…

265
28:55.463 --> 28:58.132
Call an ambulance! Now!

266
29:42.677 --> 29:46.139
YOU DID GOOD, INOSE

267
33:44.460 --> 33:48.381
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
